      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Queue attention request handoffs",
        "body": "Closes #9\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nFixes a race where rapid `nameplate attention ...` invocations could overwrite the single shared `attention.json` handoff file before the app consumed it.\r\n\r\nAttention requests now write to a queue directory using unique timestamp/UUID filenames. The app drains queued requests deterministically and still consumes the legacy `attention.json` path for migration compatibility.\r\n\r\nThe app-side display path now keeps an in-memory queue and shows attention alerts sequentially, so draining multiple files does not immediately replace earlier alerts.\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\n- `swift build`\r\n- `git diff --check`\r\n\r\nDirect proof against the built `NameplateCore` module:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nPROOF files-after-write count=2 names=attention-1800000000000000-00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001.json,attention-1800000000001000-00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002.json\r\nPROOF consumed count=2 messages=first,second\r\nPROOF files-after-consume count=0\r\n```",
        "branch": "fix/issue-9-attention-request-queue",
